                                        "entry_id": "dc945e31-2102-3bf9-a432-3d8d6be15e6b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A histamine H₂-receptor antagonist that inhibits the production of acid in the stomach, mainly used to treat heartburn and peptic ulcers, but notorious for causing male impotence. It is a histamine analog, a sulfur-containing derivative of imidazole."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ceeef873-b664-4530-9d1c-86c7a2296259",
                                                "sense_id": "f8318ea5-f758-3eb5-99d5-a486d5a9e4dd",
                                                "text": "Until Tagamet (cimetidine), most major drug companies didn't take tummy troubles terribly seriously."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
